# Configuration parity

Every runtime configuration change must keep the host, MSI and `/config` aligned.
This applies to additions, renames, removals, defaults, types, enum values,
validation, feature gates, module dependencies and persistence behavior.

- Update host options, JSON binding and validation together with the MSI's
  interactive controls, silent-install properties, settings-writing logic and
  module/feature metadata. Every affected setting must be available to MSI users.
- Ensure the localhost `/config` page exposes every affected setting with a
  usable editor, including disabled modules, nested options, lists, flags and
  credentials. Update field metadata/components when automatic rendering cannot
  represent the type correctly; preserve localhost and secret-handling protections.
- Check both directions: setup-written values must load correctly in `/config`,
  and UI-saved values must bind correctly on restart and survive MSI repair and
  upgrade according to the documented installer ownership rules. Preserve
  unrelated JSON sections and plugin settings.
- Keep types, accepted values, validation and dependencies consistent. Document
  and test deliberate differences in MSI versus host defaults and which keys the
  installer owns. State whether a change requires a service restart.
- Add or update meaningful coverage for host validation, MSI interactive/silent
  persistence and repair/upgrade merging, and UI exposure/edit/save round trips.
  Verify actual field availability and editing; reflection or generic JSON
  support alone is insufficient. Check renamed/removed settings for stale controls,
  properties, metadata and documentation.
- Update `docs/configuration.md`, `docs/windows-service.md` and affected security,
  troubleshooting, README and `site/` guidance. Regenerate configuration catalogs
  with `VESTIGO_REGENERATE_DOCS=1`, then verify tests without that variable.
- Report any unverified MSI/UI path or environment-dependent skip explicitly.
  A setting implemented only in JSON is not a completed configuration change.
